# Answer key for t1_breadth.sql - B1 core SELECT, breadth.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE. A key written after
# seeing the output records what the analyser did, not what is true.
#
# Conventions: OBJECTIVES.md "Labelling conventions", plus D-9, D-10 and D-11 (decided
# 2026-10-01, NOT yet implemented - every fact resting on them is expected to score as a
# miss or a false positive until they are, and the report says which).
#
# Every relation is schema-qualified, so no context_dependent_binding boundary is
# expected. All facts are band 0: no PL/pgSQL in this file.
#
# FLAGGED, NOT LABELLED (a convention question for the batch report, not a key decision):
#   * S10a - GROUPING(region, country_code) inside the CASE that writes `level`. It reports
#     which grouping set a row belongs to and carries no column's value. Nothing is labelled
#     for `level` and nothing is forbidden, so whatever the analyser emits there is
#     reported, not scored as right or wrong by fiat.
#   * S8a / S8b - the merged column of USING / NATURAL is labelled from the LEFT input only,
#     which is PostgreSQL's definition for an inner join. The right input's equal column is
#     neither labelled nor forbidden: equal by construction, so an edge from it is
#     redundant rather than false.

@ 23 S1 projections and expressions
value staging.products.id -> mart.product_performance.product_id identity
value staging.products.brand, staging.products.sku -> mart.product_performance.category_name derived
note COALESCE(brand, 'n/a') has one column argument: a null guard, so derived, not conditional.
value staging.products.created_at -> mart.product_performance.period_month derived
value staging.products.list_price -> mart.product_performance.revenue derived
value staging.products.list_price, staging.products.cost -> mart.product_performance.margin derived
# Relabelled 2026-10-02 under D-19 (B4-02): was `conditional`. NULLIF(x, 0) reads one column.
value staging.products.cost -> mart.product_performance.revenue_share derived
value staging.products.list_price -> mart.product_performance.revenue_share derived
note D-7: cost passes through NULLIF on its path, list_price does not.
value staging.products.list_price, staging.products.cost -> mart.product_performance.running_revenue conditional
value staging.products.cost -> mart.product_performance.prev_month_revenue derived
value staging.products.status, staging.products.list_price -> mart.product_performance.growth_pct conditional
forbid value staging.products.brand -> mart.product_performance.category_name conditional | a one-column COALESCE is a null guard, not a choice between sources

@ 46 S2 WHERE
value staging.customers.country_code -> mart.top_customers.region identity
value staging.customers.id -> mart.top_customers.customer_id identity
value staging.customers.full_name -> mart.top_customers.full_name identity
filter staging.customers.status, staging.customers.segment, staging.customers.signup_ts, staging.customers.email, staging.customers.full_name, staging.customers.attributes, staging.customers.country_code, staging.customers.created_at -> mart.top_customers
note created_at < signup_ts compares two columns of ONE relation: not a join, so both are filters.

@ 68 S3 INNER JOIN, multi-condition ON
value staging.orders.order_ts -> mart.channel_mix.period_month derived
value staging.orders.channel -> mart.channel_mix.channel identity
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.channel_mix.region identity
value staging.order_lines.order_id -> mart.channel_mix.orders identity
value staging.order_lines.quantity, staging.order_lines.unit_price -> mart.channel_mix.revenue derived
value staging.order_lines.discount_pct -> mart.channel_mix.share_of_region derived
forbid filter staging.orders.status -> mart.channel_mix | a literal predicate inside ON is still part of the join, structural under D-5
forbid filter staging.orders.id -> mart.channel_mix | a join key in ON is structural (D-5)

@ 89 S4a LEFT JOIN, right-side predicate in ON
value core.dim_carrier.id -> mart.carrier_scorecard.carrier_id identity
value core.dim_carrier.name -> mart.carrier_scorecard.carrier_name identity
value staging.shipments.id -> mart.carrier_scorecard.shipments identity
forbid filter staging.shipments.status -> mart.carrier_scorecard | in a LEFT JOIN's ON it decides which shipments match; every carrier is kept

@ 106 S4b LEFT JOIN, the same predicate in WHERE
value core.dim_carrier.mode -> mart.kpi_rollup.region identity
value core.dim_carrier.status -> mart.kpi_rollup.segment identity
value staging.shipments.id -> mart.kpi_rollup.orders identity
value staging.shipments.cost -> mart.kpi_rollup.revenue identity
filter staging.shipments.status -> mart.kpi_rollup

@ 122 S5 RIGHT JOIN
value staging.orders.created_at -> mart.sales_daily.sale_date derived
value staging.orders.store_id -> mart.sales_daily.store_id identity
value staging.payments.method -> mart.sales_daily.region identity
value staging.orders.id -> mart.sales_daily.orders identity
value staging.payments.amount -> mart.sales_daily.gross_amount identity
value staging.orders.amount -> mart.sales_daily.net_amount identity

@ 140 S6 FULL OUTER JOIN with COALESCE over the keys
value staging.fx_rates.rate_date, staging.payments.paid_at -> mart.channel_mix.period_month conditional
value staging.fx_rates.currency, staging.payments.currency -> mart.channel_mix.channel conditional
value staging.payments.amount, staging.fx_rates.rate_to_usd -> mart.channel_mix.revenue derived
forbid filter staging.payments.currency -> mart.channel_mix | a FULL JOIN's ON keeps every row from both sides; it removes nothing

@ 156 S7 CROSS JOIN to a one-row derived table
value core.dim_store.region -> mart.top_customers.region identity
value core.dim_store.id -> mart.top_customers.customer_id identity
value core.dim_store.name -> mart.top_customers.full_name identity
value core.dim_date.fiscal_year -> mart.top_customers.position derived
filter core.dim_date.calendar_date -> mart.top_customers
note A filter inside a derived table still decides what lands in the written relation.

@ 176 S8a JOIN USING
