@ 285 S11 string_agg, array_agg, FILTER, WITHIN GROUP
value core.fct_shipment.carrier_id -> mart.carrier_scorecard.carrier_id identity
value core.fct_shipment.status -> mart.carrier_scorecard.carrier_name aggregated
influence core.fct_shipment.shipped_date -> mart.carrier_scorecard.carrier_name
note string_agg's own ORDER BY decides the order of the pieces; no part of shipped_date is in the string.
value core.fct_shipment.shipped_date -> mart.carrier_scorecard.period_month aggregated
value core.fct_shipment.order_id -> mart.carrier_scorecard.shipments aggregated
value core.fct_shipment.delivered_date, core.fct_shipment.promised_date -> mart.carrier_scorecard.on_time_pct aggregated
note D-10: the FILTER columns of COUNT(*) are value sources of that one column.
value core.fct_shipment.transit_days, core.fct_shipment.warehouse_id -> mart.carrier_scorecard.avg_transit_days aggregated
value core.fct_shipment.transit_days -> mart.carrier_scorecard.p50_transit_days, mart.carrier_scorecard.p90_transit_days aggregated
note WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY transit_days): for a percentile the ordered column IS the value.
value core.fct_shipment.weight_kg -> mart.carrier_scorecard.p90_transit_days aggregated
value core.fct_shipment.cost, core.fct_shipment.weight_kg -> mart.carrier_scorecard.cost_per_kg aggregated
influence core.fct_shipment.carrier_id -> mart.carrier_scorecard.carrier_name, mart.carrier_scorecard.period_month, mart.carrier_scorecard.shipments, mart.carrier_scorecard.on_time_pct, mart.carrier_scorecard.avg_transit_days, mart.carrier_scorecard.p50_transit_days, mart.carrier_scorecard.p90_transit_days, mart.carrier_scorecard.cost_per_kg
forbid filter core.fct_shipment.warehouse_id -> mart.carrier_scorecard | FILTER (WHERE) changes one aggregate's value, not which rows the table holds (D-10)
forbid filter core.fct_shipment.weight_kg -> mart.carrier_scorecard | FILTER (WHERE) changes one aggregate's value, not which rows the table holds (D-10)
forbid filter core.fct_shipment.delivered_date -> mart.carrier_scorecard | FILTER (WHERE) changes one aggregate's value, not which rows the table holds (D-10)

@ 312 S12 window functions
value core.fct_order_line.product_key -> mart.product_performance.product_id identity
value core.fct_order_line.channel -> mart.product_performance.category_name derived
note FIRST_VALUE picks a value out of the window: derived, never aggregated (D-3).
value core.fct_order_line.order_date -> mart.product_performance.period_month identity
value core.fct_order_line.net_amount -> mart.product_performance.revenue aggregated
value core.fct_order_line.gross_amount -> mart.product_performance.running_revenue aggregated
value core.fct_order_line.net_amount -> mart.product_performance.prev_month_revenue derived
value core.fct_order_line.quantity -> mart.product_performance.growth_pct derived
influence core.fct_order_line.product_key, core.fct_order_line.order_date -> mart.product_performance.category_name, mart.product_performance.units, mart.product_performance.revenue, mart.product_performance.running_revenue, mart.product_performance.prev_month_revenue, mart.product_performance.growth_pct
note `units` is ROW_NUMBER() OVER w: no value source at all, only its window's influence.
influence core.fct_order_line.store_id, core.fct_order_line.gross_amount -> mart.product_performance.margin
influence core.fct_order_line.amount_usd -> mart.product_performance.revenue_share
forbid value core.fct_order_line.gross_amount -> mart.product_performance.margin | RANK's ORDER BY decides the rank; no part of gross_amount is in it (D-4)
forbid value core.fct_order_line.amount_usd -> mart.product_performance.revenue_share | NTILE's ORDER BY decides the bucket; no part of amount_usd is in it (D-4)

@ 343 S13a DISTINCT
